      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The consensus across major platforms is that \"punching up\" is generally protected, but targeting a specific protected group with dehumanizing material usually constitutes hate speech regardless of the satirical intent. When assessing real-world harm, teams often weigh whether the content relies on objective hyperbole to criticize power or makes unsubstantiated, harmful claims that could incite violence or discrimination against that group. Since internal moderators often view their intent as subjective, most organizations now explicitly prohibit framing content that impersonates or attacks identity as satire to avoid liability.",
